# Thranduil's Decree: a permanent spell is judged as it is on the stack. Bot2 casts Bilbo Baggins as its Adventure, Take a Glance (a sorcery on the stack, CR 715.3):
# countered, it is not a permanent spell, so the card goes to Bot2's graveyard, not exile (and is not the Adventure's exile either: it never resolved). Then a
# Prowling Serpopard, a permanent spell that can't be countered, is cast: the Decree does not counter it, so it is not exiled and Bot2 keeps it as it resolves.
# (Bot1 casts the Decree twice, a second one in hand.)

